  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef pytorch_lstm_cell_from_scratch(x: list, h_prev: list, c_prev: list, W: list, b: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **LSTM Cell from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef pytorch_lstm_cell_from_scratch(x: list, h_prev: list, c_prev: list, W: list, b: list) -> dict:\n    xt, hp, cp = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(h_prev, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(c_prev, dtype=torch.float32)\n    gates = torch.matmul(torch.tensor(W, dtype=torch.float32), torch.cat([xt, hp])) + torch.tensor(b, dtype=torch.float32)\n    H = len(hp)\n    i, f, c, o = torch.sigmoid(gates[:H]), torch.sigmoid(gates[H:2*H]), torch.tanh(gates[2*H:3*H]), torch.sigmoid(gates[3*H:4*H])\n    c_n = f * cp + i * c\n    h_n = o * torch.tanh(c_n)\n    return {'h_next': [round(float(v), 4) for v in h_n.tolist()], 'c_next': [round(float(v), 4) for v in c_n.tolist()]}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
